d.plnkr.co/tUMGOtW39iMDYKHcv1hm/?layout=!@#$%^&*()\r\n\r\nError found : \r\nURIError: URI malformed\r\n    at decodeURIComponent (<anonymous>)\r\n    at Ye (vendor.6b9be0480d04ab9c9c6c.js:6)\r\n    at tn.$$parse (vendor.6b9be0480d04ab9c9c6c.js:6)\r\n    at tn.$$parseLinkUrl (vendor.6b9be0480d04ab9c9c6c.js:6)\r\n    at an.$get (vendor.6b9be0480d04ab9c9c6c.js:6)\r\n    at Object.a [as invoke] (vendor.6b9be0480d04ab9c9c6c.js:6)\r\n    at vendor.6b9be0480d04ab9c9c6c.js:6\r\n    at r (vendor.6b9be0480d04ab9c9c6c.js:6)\r\n    at i (vendor.6b9be0480d04ab9c9c6c.js:6)\r\n    at Object.a [as invoke] (vendor.6b9be0480d04ab9c9c6c.js:6)\r\n\r\n## What is the motivation / use case for changing the behavior?\r\n<!-- Describe the motivation or the concrete use case. -->\r\nBy fixing this issue adding % in the URL will not crush the application \r\n\r\n## Environment\r\n\r\n<pre><code>\r\nAngular version: 4.0.0\r\n<!-- Check whether this is still an issue in the most recent Angular version -->\r\n\r\nBrowser:\r\n- [ X ] Chrome (desktop) version 63.0.3239.132\r\n- [ ] Chrome (Android) version XX\r\n- [ ] Chrome (iOS) version XX\r\n- [ ] Firefox version XX\r\n- [ ] Safari (desktop) version XX\r\n- [ ] Safari (iOS) version XX\r\n- [ ] IE version XX\r\n- [ ] Edge version XX\r\n \r\nFor Tooling issues:\r\n- Node version: XX  <!-- run `node --version` -->\r\n- Platform:  <!-- Mac, Linux, Windows -->\r\n\r\nOthers:\r\n<!-- Anything else relevant?  Operating system version, IDE, package manager, HTTP server, ... -->\r\n</code></pre>\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"mhevery","id":111951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTk1MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhevery","html_url":"https://github.com/mhevery","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhevery/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhevery/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhevery/gists{/gist_id}","starre